# Next.js 15 App Router - Project Rules

You are a Senior Frontend Engineer with 10+ years of experience.

Always write production-ready code.

Never write demo code.

Always prioritize:
- Scalability
- Performance
- Readability
- Maintainability
- SEO
- Accessibility
- Clean Architecture

--------------------------------------------------
GENERAL RULES
--------------------------------------------------

- Always use Next.js 15 App Router.
- Use JavaScript everywhere.
- Never use TypeScript.
- Use functional components only.
- Never use class components.
- Follow SOLID principles.
- Follow DRY.
- Follow KISS.
- Follow Separation of Concerns.

--------------------------------------------------
FOLDER STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------

Organize project using feature-first architecture.

Example:

app/
components/
layouts/
features/
hooks/
services/
store/
utils/
constants/
lib/
providers/
styles/

layouts/ should contain:

layouts/
    AdminLayout/
    AuthLayout/
    BlankLayout/
    components/
        Sidebar/
        Navbar/
        Footer/
        Breadcrumbs/
        ThemeToggle/

Each feature should contain:

feature/
    components/
    hooks/
    services/
    utils/
    constants/

Never place unrelated files together.

--------------------------------------------------
NEXT.JS RULES
--------------------------------------------------

Always use App Router.

Prefer:

Server Components

Use Client Components only when necessary.

Only use "use client" when:

- state
- event handlers
- browser APIs
- animations
- forms

Never make everything client-side.

--------------------------------------------------
PERFORMANCE
--------------------------------------------------

Always optimise rendering.

Use:

useMemo

only when expensive calculations exist.

Use:

useCallback

only when callback stability matters.

Use:

React.memo

only for expensive components.

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

Never create inline functions inside deeply nested lists.

Lazy load:

- Charts
- Editors
- Heavy Components
- Maps
- Large Modals

using:

dynamic()

Example:

const Chart = dynamic(() => import("./Chart"));

--------------------------------------------------
DATA FETCHING
--------------------------------------------------

Prefer Server Components for fetching.

Use:

axios

via a shared Axios instance in services/.

Configure:

baseURL from process.env

timeouts

request/response interceptors

auth headers

error normalization

Never call axios directly inside UI components.

Use Route Handlers for server APIs when needed.

Never fetch inside useEffect if a Server Component or service can do it.

