--------------------------------------------------
LIGHT AND DARK MODE
--------------------------------------------------

Support light, dark, and system themes.

Use:

next-themes

with Tailwind class-based dark mode.

Setup:

- Wrap the app with a ThemeProvider in providers/
- Place ThemeProvider in the root layout
- Use attribute="class" so Tailwind dark: works
- Set defaultTheme to "system"
- Enable enableSystem
- Disable transitions on change when needed to avoid flicker

Prevent flash of incorrect theme:

- Suppress hydration mismatch on the html element when required
- Never hardcode theme only on the client after paint
- Apply the theme class before first paint

Persistence:

- Persist user preference (localStorage via next-themes)
- Respect prefers-color-scheme when theme is "system"

Colors:

- Define semantic CSS variables for both themes
  Examples: --background, --foreground, --muted, --border, --primary
- Use variables in Tailwind theme tokens
- Never hardcode light-only or dark-only hex/rgb in components
- Never use raw text-black / bg-white as permanent theme colors

UI rules:

- Every screen must be readable in light and dark mode
- Meet WCAG contrast in both themes
- Icons, borders, shadows, and images must adapt to both themes
- Prefer theme-aware assets or CSS filters only when necessary
- Theme toggle must be keyboard accessible and have an aria-label

Toggle:

- Provide a ThemeToggle client component
- Support light, dark, and system options
- Keep toggle logic in a small client component only
- Do not make entire layouts client-side only for theming

Do not:

- Rely on media prefers-color-scheme alone without a user override
- Duplicate theme state in Redux
- Scatter theme logic across unrelated components

