--------------------------------------------------
ADMIN UI AND LAYOUT
--------------------------------------------------

UI/UX reference:

Vuexy-style Next.js admin template
https://demos.pixinvent.com/vuexy-nextjs-admin-template/demo-1/en/dashboards/analytics

Build a modern admin dashboard UI matching this layout style:
responsive shell, collapsible sidebar, sticky navbar, card-based content, and full light/dark support.

Do not copy proprietary Vuexy assets, code, or branding.
Match the structure, spacing, and interaction patterns only.

--------------------------------------------------
APP SHELL
--------------------------------------------------

Use a dedicated AdminLayout for authenticated pages.

Structure:

AdminLayout
    Sidebar
    Navbar
    main content
    Footer (optional)

Requirements:

- Full-height app shell (min-h-screen)
- Fixed or sticky left Sidebar
- Sticky top Navbar
- Scrollable main content area only
- Consistent content padding
- Soft surface background behind content cards
- Smooth width transition when sidebar collapses

Layout variants:

- AdminLayout: dashboards, tables, settings, CRUD pages
- AuthLayout: login, register, forgot password (split illustration + form on desktop)
- BlankLayout: error pages, simple standalone screens

Never rebuild sidebar/navbar inside individual pages.

--------------------------------------------------
SIDEBAR
--------------------------------------------------

Sidebar must include:

- Brand logo + product name
- Scrollable nav menu
- Nested/collapsible menu groups
- Active route highlight
- Icons + labels
- Collapse / expand control

Behavior:

- Desktop: expanded by default
- Desktop collapsed: icon-only rail
- Tablet/Mobile: off-canvas drawer overlay
- Close drawer on route change (mobile)
- Persist collapsed state when useful
- Keyboard accessible open/close
- Escape closes mobile drawer
- Focus trap while mobile drawer is open

Do not:

- Hide navigation without a hamburger/menu control on mobile
- Use page-level custom sidebars

--------------------------------------------------
NAVBAR
--------------------------------------------------

Sticky top Navbar must include:

- Sidebar toggle (hamburger)
- Optional search
- Theme toggle (light / dark / system)
- Notifications (optional)
- User avatar menu (profile, settings, logout)

Behavior:

- Align with content width
- Remain usable when sidebar is collapsed
- Never overflow on mobile
- Icon buttons need aria-label
- Dropdowns must work with keyboard

--------------------------------------------------
CONTENT AND DASHBOARD UI
--------------------------------------------------

Page content pattern:

- Optional breadcrumbs
- Page title + short description/actions
- Responsive card/widget grid
- Tables, charts, filters inside content cards

Card style:

- Rounded corners
- Subtle border or soft shadow
- Theme-aware background/surface
- Consistent internal padding
- Clear hierarchy: title, value, supporting text, action

Dashboard grids:

- Mobile: 1 column
- Tablet: 2 columns
- Desktop: 3–4 columns where appropriate
- Use CSS grid/flex with gap
- Avoid cramped widgets
- Charts and heavy widgets: lazy load with dynamic()

Tables:

- Responsive (horizontal scroll or stacked rows on small screens)
- Sticky header when useful
- Pagination, sorting, filtering

--------------------------------------------------
VISUAL SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------

Follow Vuexy-like visual language:

- Clean sans-serif UI typography
- Primary accent color for active states, links, primary buttons
- Semantic colors: success, warning, error, info
- Soft surfaces, muted borders, light elevation
- Comfortable spacing (consistent scale)
- Rounded interactive controls

Theme tokens required:

--background
--foreground
--surface
--surface-elevated
--muted
--border
--primary
--primary-foreground
--success
--warning
--error
--info
--sidebar
--sidebar-foreground
--navbar

All layout chrome (sidebar, navbar, cards, inputs, tables) must use these tokens in both light and dark mode.

